{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Is not this the thing that we spoke to you in Egypt, saying.</b> Rashi explained: and where did they speak? ״יֵרֶא ה׳ עֲלֵיכֶם וְיִשְׁפֹּט״ (Exodus 5:21). And his explanation itself needs explanation, for here they said ״כִּי טוֹב לָנוּ עֲבֹד אֶת מִצְרַיִם מִמּוּתֵנוּ בַּמִּדְבָּר״, whereas there they said ״יֵרֶא ה׳ עֲלֵיכֶם וְיִשְׁפֹּט אֲשֶׁר הִבְאַשְׁתֶּם אֶת רֵיחֵנוּ בְּעֵינֵי פַרְעֹה וּבְעֵינֵי עֲבָדָיו לָתֵת חֶרֶב בְּיָדָם לְהָרְגֵנוּ״ (Exodus 5:21). And this they said surely concerning the additional labor, which was likened to a sword — but what is the difference between a sword and death? Also what they said there, ״לָתֵת חֶרֶב בְּיָדָם,״ needs explanation, for Pharaoh did not seek to kill them by the sword but only to make their labor heavier upon them. And it appears to me that Israel said to Moses a twofold complaint: for now he has not sent us off and has made his labor heavier because you made our odor foul in his eyes — this is one thing, and yet another: even if you say that he will send us off after all, we will be escapees, for you said to him in the name of HaShem ״שַׁלַּח עַמִּי וְיָחֹגּוּ לִי בַּמִּדְבָּר״ (Exodus 5:1), and when it becomes known to him that we are escaping, then without doubt he will pursue after us with the sword, and in this respect it is as though you gave a sword into his hand to kill us and put us to death. And this is what they said here, for they had already said to him in Egypt ״כִּי טוֹב לָנוּ עֲבֹד אֶת מִצְרַיִם מִמּוּתֵנוּ בַּמִּדְבָּר,״ because they had already said to him ״לָתֵת חֶרֶב בְּיָדָם לְהָרְגֵנוּ״ (Exodus 5:21). And they said this concerning the fact that in the end he would pursue after them with the sword in the wilderness and put them to death." "And there are some who explain by way of jest: 'Is not this the thing that we spoke' — now; 'in Egypt' is where we should have said thus, and not now, for our time has passed. And this is what it says, ״בְּמִצְרַיִם לֵאמֹר״ — meaning, there is where we should have said 'Leave us alone' and so forth — but we did not say it."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:08.035767867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}